omr-vps-admin (0.18+20261002) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix SIP ALG never being applied when enabled, logged only as a recurring "nft apply failed: Error: Could not process rule: No such file or directory (x2)" at every start and every /sipalg push from the router: the explicit modprobe nf_conntrack_sip added for #4361 runs inside omr-admin.service, whose CapabilityBoundingSet lacked CAP_SYS_MODULE, so it failed with EPERM, the sip_udp/sip_tcp ct helper objects were never created and the ct_helpers rules referencing them were refused. CAP_SYS_MODULE is added to the bounding set, and a failed modprobe is now logged with its own error ("SIP ALG not applied, can't load nf_conntrack_sip: ...") and stops there instead of running nft batches that can only fail
  * Add a unit test for the modprobe failure path of _nft_sync_sipalg (test/test_nft.py)
  * Refuse usernames starting with a dot: USERNAME_PATTERN accepted '.' and '..', and usernames end up in file names under /etc/openvpn/ccd, the OpenVPN PKI and /var/opt/openmptcprouter, so '..' as a username pointed those paths at the parent directory. The first character must now be a letter, a digit, '_' or '-'
  * Build every file path that contains a username, interface name or router-supplied file name through a new safe_path_join(), which refuses any result outside its base directory: /lan's OpenVPN ccd file, the easyrsa req/key/crt paths of /add_user and /remove_user, /backuppost, /backupget, /backuplist and the /sys/class/net statistics read. /backuppost answers 'Invalid username' and /backupget 'Invalid filename' instead of writing or reading outside the backup directory
  * Fix /backuplist and the backup rotation of /backuppost matching other users' backups: the glob was <username>*-backup.tar.gz, so user 'bob' saw (and rotated away) the backups of 'bobby'. The username is now glob-escaped and followed by '-'
  * remove_ss_go_user() validates the username and URL-encodes it before putting it in the shadowsocks-go API path, so a crafted name can no longer reach another API route
  * Stop relaying exception texts to API clients: mqvpn_api() returned str(e) of a socket or JSON error, which /mqvpn* endpoints passed on as-is, and /metrics/engine did the same with InfluxDB fetch errors. They now return a fixed message and log the details at debug level
  * Pass every user-supplied value logged by omr-admin (usernames, MPTCP scheduler and path manager names, firewall entry fields, MQVPN API errors) through log_safe(), which escapes CR and LF so a request can't forge extra lines in the log, and in particular can't fake the authentication failure line fail2ban watches
  * Userids taken from the config or the query string are converted to int before being used in a file name (/status, /config, /vxlan, /glorytun, /dsvpn, /vpnips and the Glorytun/DSVPN helpers)
  * Exceptions swallowed while adding XRay outbounds and GRE tunnels are now logged at debug level instead of silently ignored
  * MPTCPServer falls back to 127.0.0.1 instead of 0.0.0.0 when no host is configured, mirroring uvicorn's own default rather than exposing the API on every interface
  * Close every file handle opened for an MD5 check or a config read: file_as_bytes() now takes a path and opens it in a with block, a new read_first_line() reads the Glorytun and DSVPN keys, and mlvpn/WireGuard configs are read in a with block. Previously each of these leaked an open file descriptor until garbage collection
  * Remove dead code: unused variables, unreachable commented-out blocks (/backupshow, /backupedit, old xray restarts, GRE tunnel parsing), the unused FileResponse import, the meaningless verify=False on plain HTTP SoftEther API calls, and fix swapped "add"/"remove" SoftEther debug messages
  * cypthon.py makes the compiled omr-admin binary mode 0700 instead of 0755
  * Clean up the test suite (unused imports and fixtures, a duplicated TestGetMetricsHistory class name hiding the first one) and add unit tests for safe_path_join, log_safe and the new username pattern (test/test_api.py); the MQVPN control API test now checks that the exception text is not returned

