omr-vps-admin (0.18+20260924) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Accept ipproto='any' on /shorewall, /shorewalllist, /shorewallopen and /shorewallclose (and their /firewall* names): LuCI's "Restrict to address family = IPv4 and IPv6" stores family='any' in uci and the router's _vps_firewall_redirect_port passes that value straight into the API call, but the IPPROTO enum only knew ipv4 and ipv6, so the POST came back 422 Unprocessable Content, the port was never opened and nothing noticed -- the router never looks at the result of _set_json. 'any' now means both families: /shorewallopen writes a v4 and a v6 rule, /shorewallclose removes both, /shorewall toggles bulk_redirect_v4 and bulk_redirect_v6 together, and /shorewalllist returns both families' lines, deduplicated because the legacy line layout the router greps has no family column and a port opened for both would otherwise be listed twice and closed on the line it did not match
  * Stop reading anything that is not literally 'ipv4' as IPv6 in those four handlers: with 'any' rejected by the enum that was unreachable, but it is what made the address family a two-way branch in the first place; each one now resolves the value through _fw_families() and acts on every family it covers
  * On /shorewallopen with ipproto='any', an address restriction pins the rule to the family of that literal (source_dip/source_ip): a v6 copy of a rule restricted to an IPv4 address renders `meta nfproto ipv6 ip6 daddr 1.2.3.4`, which nft refuses, and user_accept/user_dnat are flushed in a single nft transaction, so that one rule would have dropped every opened port of every user. _render_fw_ports() skips such an entry and logs it rather than failing the whole flush, which also covers entries already stored by an earlier version
  * Add unit tests for the new family handling: /shorewallopen with 'any' opening both families and staying IPv4 when restricted to an IPv4 address, /shorewallclose removing DNAT and ACCEPT for both, /shorewall setting both bulk toggles (test/test_api.py), /shorewalllist listing both families without duplicates and _render_fw_ports skipping a rule restricted to the other family (test/test_nft.py)

