omr-vps-admin (0.18+20260923) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a scheduler pushed by the router reaching the upload direction only, on a VPS where the proxy is shadowsocks-go (the default for shadowsocks-rust/-go routers): an MPTCP socket keeps the scheduler its listener had when it was created, so writing net.mptcp.scheduler into /etc/sysctl.d/90-shadowsocks.conf and applying the sysctl never reaches the listeners already running, which is why POST /mptcp restarts every service that terminates MPTCP here once the file really changed. shadowsocks-libev, v2ray, xray, glorytun-tcp and openvpn were on that list but shadowsocks-go never was, so a router selecting e.g. bpf_red for redundancy got it on everything it sent and silently kept the previous scheduler on everything the server sent back, until the next unrelated restart of shadowsocks-go. /etc/shadowsocks-go/server.json now gets shadowsocks-go.service restarted like the others, and the restart block carries a comment saying why it has to exist at all
  * Add unit tests for the /mptcp restart list: shadowsocks-go restarted when it is installed, left alone when its config file is absent, all six MPTCP listeners restarted when they are all present, and nothing restarted at all when 90-shadowsocks.conf comes out identical (test/test_api.py)

