omr-vps-admin (0.18+20260910) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix every boot logging "sysctl: setting key 'net.mptcp.path_manager': Couldn't write 'fullmesh'... ignoring: No such file or directory" and MPTCP silently staying on whatever path manager the kernel defaulted to: the router sends network.globals.mptcp_path_manager verbatim and that option still carries the out-of-tree v0.95 vocabulary (default/fullmesh/ndiffports/binder), while a mainline kernel registers exactly two path managers, 'kernel' and 'userspace' (net.mptcp.available_path_managers), and rejects any other name with ENOENT. POST /mptcp now maps a v0 name onto 'kernel' -- all four of them are in-kernel path managers -- through the new normalize_mptcp_path_manager(), before the sysctl call and before the value is persisted into 90-shadowsocks.conf, so the line stops failing at each boot
