  * Fix POST /shorewalllist (and /firewalllist) returning a free-form summary line since the nftables migration instead of the Shorewall rules-file line layout the router's openmptcprouter-vps init script still parses: _vps_firewall_redirect_port greps "<port>\t# OMR <user> redirect router <port> port <proto>" to know a port is already handled and _vps_firewall_close_port awk-splits the columns ($1 type, $2 net[:source-host], $4 proto, $5 port, $6 "-", $7 original-destination) to decide what to close, so the router re-issued /shorewallopen for every port on every set_vps_firewall pass (config rewrite + user_dnat/user_accept chain flush each time), then fired /shorewallclose with garbage columns for every line, and ports removed on the router were never closed on the VPS; _legacy_fw_line() now renders each fw_ports entry byte-compatible with what the Shorewall-era omr-admin wrote to /etc/shorewall/rules
  * /shorewalllist selects entries on the "# OMR <user> <name>" comment prefix the router asks for ("redirect router", "open router") like the Shorewall-era grep on the rules file did, instead of mapping the name to a bare ACCEPT/DNAT fwtype filter, so installer-opened services with other names never end up in the router's "close what I don't know" pass
  * Ignore /shorewallopen requests whose fwtype is neither ACCEPT nor DNAT (routers push "REDIRECT" for a traffic rule saved without a target): the Shorewall implementation wrote nothing for those, but the nftables one stored them in fw_ports forever while rendering nothing; legacy entries of that kind are pruned from fw_ports on the next open/close for the same user
  * Skip the omr-admin-config.json rewrite and the user_accept/user_dnat chain resync when /shorewallopen re-posts an entry identical to one already stored, which routers do for every known port on each reconciliation pass
  * Order omr-admin.service after nftables.service and ship an nftables.service.d drop-in (debian/omr-admin-resync.conf) whose ExecStartPost/ExecReload try-restart omr-admin, so any start, restart or reload of nftables (each re-runs /etc/nftables.conf, which begins with `flush ruleset` and thereby empties the user_accept/user_dnat/gre_snat/dscp_mark/ct_helpers chains) re-triggers _nft_resync_all() and repopulates the chains from omr-admin-config.json; previously only the VPS installer's update path restarted omr-admin after nftables, and since /shorewalllist is rendered from the persisted fw_ports rather than the live ruleset the router now treats such ports as already handled and no longer re-pushes them; postinst runs daemon-reload so the drop-in takes effect on upgrade
  * Add unit tests for the legacy line layout and the router-side grep/awk contract, the name/family selection, the unsupported-fwtype handling and the identical re-POST no-op (test/test_nft.py); document the /shorewalllist line layout in docs/api.md

